      "p0001-ocr-l0018"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "2016 MCM/ICM"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0019"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary Sheet"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0020"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "(Your team's summary should be included as the first page of your electronic submission.)"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "front_matter",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0021"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Type a summary of your results on this page. Do not include"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000020",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "front_matter",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0022"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "the name of your school, advisor, or team members on this page."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000021",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0023",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0024"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0023",
      "p0001-ocr-l0024"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "We propose a Bayesian multi-stage model to maximize Return on Investment (RI) over the next five years."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000022",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0025",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0026"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0026",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0027"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0027",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0028"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0028",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0029"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0029",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0030"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0025",
      "p0001-ocr-l0026",
      "p0001-ocr-l0027",
      "p0001-ocr-l0028",
      "p0001-ocr-l0029",
      "p0001-ocr-l0030"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "First, a model was made to relate the distribution of students' majors at a school to the expected number of jobs that that school will add to to the economy. Here, we relate the unemployment outlook in each particular discipline to the percentage of students at each school pursuing that particular course of study. In the case that a school was going to produce a high number of graduates in a field that is already oversaturated (that is, has a high unemployment rate), it is actually assigned a negative contribution to the number of jobs in the economy."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000023",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0031",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0032"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0032",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0033"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0033",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0034"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0031",
      "p0001-ocr-l0032",
      "p0001-ocr-l0033",
      "p0001-ocr-l0034"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Next, a model was fit to give the relationship between jobs added to the economy and change in real Gross Domestic Product (GDP). This was based on a linear relationship we observed between changes in logGDP and changes in unemployment, fit to data gathered beginning in 1948. This particular model has a surprisingly good fit considering the field."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000024",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0035",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0036"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0035",
      "p0001-ocr-l0036"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Each school was given a Goodness rating based on added GDP and the median salary of its alumni. Salary was simply scaled and added to GDP in order to compute this metric."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000025",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0037",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0038"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0038",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0039"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0037",
      "p0001-ocr-l0038",
      "p0001-ocr-l0039"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The centerpiece of our proposal is a linear regression model relating Goodness to a combination of the school's tuition and enrollment. This model is meant to contain general information about how a school's resources impact its Goodness."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000026",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0040",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0041"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0041",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0042"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0042",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0043"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0043",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0044"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0040",
      "p0001-ocr-l0041",
      "p0001-ocr-l0042",
      "p0001-ocr-l0043",
      "p0001-ocr-l0044"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The posteriors of this overall model are used as priors for the parameters of a series of models (these priors are injected with additional variance so as not to overwhelm the data), each one fit to a particular school. Each of these models represents a predicted relationship between a school's available funds per student and its Goodness, as well as how a change in its funds would affect its Goodness, which we call a Goodness curve."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000027",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0045",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0046"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0046",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0047"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0045",
      "p0001-ocr-l0046",
      "p0001-ocr-l0047"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "We model the investment of money in a school as increasing the \"effective tuition\" of that school, which will increase the Goodness of that school according to its Goodness curve. This change in Goodness is our proposal for measuring RoI."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000028",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0048",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0049"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0049",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0050"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0048",
      "p0001-ocr-l0049",
      "p0001-ocr-l0050"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Given this definition of RoI, we are presented with the question of where investments should be disbursed such that the sum of RoI is maximized: a simple optimization problem which we solve in order to obtain our results for proposal."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000029",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0051",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0052"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0051",
      "p0001-ocr-l0052"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Such curves are calculated for each year from 2016 to 2020, based on econometrics forecasts in US GDP changes and population growth."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000030",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0053",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0054"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0053",
      "p0001-ocr-l0054"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Each single stage of our model is simple, and the model in its entirety is complex rather than com- plicated. This leads to a model which, while far from trivial, is easy to interpret."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000031",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0055",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0056"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0056",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0057"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0057",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0058"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0055",
      "p0001-ocr-l0056",
      "p0001-ocr-l0057",
      "p0001-ocr-l0058"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "We present 73 schools to be funded based on our analysis. Among them are such well known schools as Princeton, Harvard, and MIT, along with a collection of other, lesser well known schools, which are expected to be as important of investment targets for the American economy according to our model. We also present the time periods during which we believe funding would be most effective."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000032",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-ocr-l0059",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-ocr-l0060"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-ocr-l0059",
      "p0001-ocr-l0060"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Data manipulation was performed in R and Python. BUGS was used for Bayesian inference on the model parameters, and R was used to solve the concomitant optimization problem."
  }
]
